IMPORT prelude

-- Private Security Industry Act 2007 (Singapore) -- who needs a licence (ss 3, 5, 6, 13, 14, 18, 19), protection of security
-- officers from assault and harassment (ss 17A to 17E), false alarms (s 20), licence validity, suspension and appeal deadlines
-- (ss 23, 24, 26), composition (s 33) and the bar on suing for fees without a licence (s 35).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSIA2007.txt, with
-- amendments to Act 23 of 2025 (in force 29 June 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the licensing gates a person or
-- business meets, the offences protecting security officers, false-alarm charges and the deadlines and caps in licensing
-- procedure. Not encoded: the private investigation agency's client-identification and record-keeping duties (ss 10, 12), security
-- assignment approvals (s 11), employee notification duties (ss 8(3), 9, 16(3), 17), the fit-and-proper factors
-- (ss 21(8), 24(11)), enforcement powers (ss 27 to 31), service of documents (s 36), the Protection from Harassment Act
-- tie-ins (s 17F), and everything left to regulations (fees, qualifications, prescribed offences, compoundable offences).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Private Security Industry Act 2007 -- licensing and protection`

§§ `3 -- persons outside the Act`

-- s 3: the Act does not apply to "(a) any member of the Singapore Police Force in the exercise of his or her functions as a police
-- officer"; (b) the SAF, (c) public officers and Government employees and (d) auxiliary police officers -- each "in the exercise of"
-- those functions; but (e) "any person appointed under the Air Navigation Act 1966 to investigate into accidents" and (f) "any person
-- appointed under the Rapid Transit Systems Act 1995 to investigate into accidents on any part of the railway" carry no such words.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a police officer`
    `a member of the Singapore Armed Forces`
    `a public officer`
    `an auxiliary police officer`
    `an appointed air accident investigator`
    `an appointed rail accident investigator`
    `a private individual`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `acting in that official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies to the person` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `a police officer` THEN NOT `acting in that official capacity`
    WHEN `a member of the Singapore Armed Forces` THEN NOT `acting in that official capacity`
    WHEN `a public officer` THEN NOT `acting in that official capacity`
    WHEN `an auxiliary police officer` THEN NOT `acting in that official capacity`
    WHEN `an appointed air accident investigator` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an appointed rail accident investigator` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5, 6, 7 -- private investigators`

-- s 5(1): "private investigator" means "any individual who, for reward, carries out any of the following functions": (a) obtaining
-- and giving information about any person; (b) searching for missing persons; (c) information as to the cause of any fire, libel,
-- loss or accident or damage to property; (d) the location or recovery of lost or stolen property; (e) "obtaining evidence to be used
-- in any civil or criminal proceedings".
-- s 5(2): does not include (a) an employee obtaining information about the employer's staff or prospective staff; (b) an employee
-- of a business entity researching another business entity for the employer's venture "or exclusively for the purposes of market
-- research"; (c) a person doing it as part of (i) law practice, (ii) public accountancy, (iii) a credit-rating business, (iv)
-- insurance or insurance adjustment -- including their employees.
DECLARE Investigation HAS
    `done by an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done for reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtaining and giving information about a person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `searching for a missing person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `finding the cause of a fire, libel, loss or accident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `locating lost or stolen property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `obtaining evidence for court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee vetting the employer's own or prospective staff` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employee researching another business for the employer or market research` IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of a law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of a public accountancy practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of a credit-rating business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `part of an insurance business or insurance adjustment` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the work` IS AN Investigation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work is a private investigator's function` IF
        `the work`'s `obtaining and giving information about a person`
    OR  `the work`'s `searching for a missing person`
    OR  `the work`'s `finding the cause of a fire, libel, loss or accident`
    OR  `the work`'s `locating lost or stolen property`
    OR  `the work`'s `obtaining evidence for court proceedings`

GIVEN `the work` IS AN Investigation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the work falls in a section 5(2) exclusion` IF
        `the work`'s `an employee vetting the employer's own or prospective staff`
    OR  `the work`'s `an employee researching another business for the employer or market research`
    OR  `the work`'s `part of a law practice`
    OR  `the work`'s `part of a public accountancy practice`
    OR  `the work`'s `part of a credit-rating business`
    OR  `the work`'s `part of an insurance business or insurance adjustment`

GIVEN `the work` IS AN Investigation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is acting as a private investigator` IF
        `the work`'s `done by an individual`
    AND `the work`'s `done for reward`
    AND `the work is a private investigator's function` `the work`
    AND (NOT `the work falls in a section 5(2) exclusion` `the work`)

-- s 6(1): a person must not "(a) carry out for reward ... any function of a private investigator; or (b) advertise, or in any way
-- hold out" willingness to do so, "except under and in accordance with a private investigator's licence". (2) $10,000 or 2 years.
-- Reading s 6(1)(a) with s 5(2): an excluded person carries out no "function of a private investigator" (an inference from
-- "for the purposes of this Act, a private investigator does not include").
GIVEN `the work` IS AN Investigation, `advertises as a private investigator` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a private investigator's licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6 is contravened` IF
        (`the person is acting as a private investigator` `the work` OR `advertises as a private investigator`)
    AND (NOT `holds a private investigator's licence`)

§§ `13, 14, 16 -- security officers`

-- s 13: "security officer" means "any individual who, for reward" (a) patrols or guards another person's property, including cash in
-- transit, physically or electronically; (b) keeps another's property under surveillance; (c) acts "as a bodyguard or bouncer"; (d)
-- "in respect of any public place or other premises and as part of his or her regular duties", screens individuals seeking entry;
-- (e) regulates traffic under the Road Traffic Act 1961.
-- s 2: a "bouncer" performs, at a place of entertainment "as part of his or her regular duties", for reward, screening, controlling
-- behaviour or removing individuals.
DECLARE Guarding HAS
    `done by an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `done for reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `guarding another person's property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `watching another person's property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acting as a bodyguard or bouncer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `screening entrants as a regular duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulating traffic` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the job` IS A Guarding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is acting as a security officer` IF
        `the job`'s `done by an individual`
    AND `the job`'s `done for reward`
    AND (    `the job`'s `guarding another person's property`
         OR  `the job`'s `watching another person's property`
         OR  `the job`'s `acting as a bodyguard or bouncer`
         OR  `the job`'s `screening entrants as a regular duty`
         OR  `the job`'s `regulating traffic`)

-- s 14(1): no one may carry out for reward any function of a security officer, or hold out, "except under and in accordance with
-- a security officer's licence". (2) $10,000 or 2 years.
GIVEN `the job` IS A Guarding, `holds a security officer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14 is contravened` IF
    `the person is acting as a security officer` `the job` AND (NOT `holds a security officer's licence`)

-- s 16(1): "A person must not employ another person as a security officer unless the other person is a licensed security officer."
-- s 8(1) says the same of private investigators. Both carry $50,000 or 2 years -- five times the fine on the unlicensed worker.
GIVEN `employs someone as a security officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the employee is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer contravenes section 16` IF
    `employs someone as a security officer` AND (NOT `the employee is licensed`)

-- Maximum fines, in dollars, from the penalty subsections.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `acting as an unlicensed private investigator`
    `running an unlicensed private investigation agency`
    `employing an unlicensed private investigator`
    `acting as an unlicensed security officer`
    `running an unlicensed security agency`
    `employing an unlicensed security officer`
    `providing an unlicensed security service`
    `breaching a licence condition`
    `assaulting a security officer`
    `hurting a security officer`
    `harassing a security officer`
    `giving a false alarm`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as an unlicensed private investigator` THEN 10000
    WHEN `running an unlicensed private investigation agency` THEN 50000
    WHEN `employing an unlicensed private investigator` THEN 50000
    WHEN `acting as an unlicensed security officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `running an unlicensed security agency` THEN 50000
    WHEN `employing an unlicensed security officer` THEN 50000
    WHEN `providing an unlicensed security service` THEN 10000
    WHEN `breaching a licence condition` THEN 10000
    WHEN `assaulting a security officer` THEN 7500
    WHEN `hurting a security officer` THEN 10000
    WHEN `harassing a security officer` THEN 5000
    WHEN `giving a false alarm` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `hurting a security officer` THEN 60
    WHEN `harassing a security officer` THEN 12
    WHEN `giving a false alarm` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 24

§§ `17A to 17E -- protecting security officers`

-- s 17A(1): an individual who assaults or uses criminal force on a person (a) "in the execution of the target person's duty as a
-- security officer"; (b) to prevent or deter that duty; or (c) in consequence of the lawful discharge of it -- $7,500 or 2 years.
-- s 17B: voluntarily causing hurt in the same circumstances -- $10,000 or 5 years.
-- s 17E: "No offence is committed ... unless the individual knows or ought reasonably to know that the target person ... was at the
-- material time a security officer and acting in that capacity."
GIVEN `assaulted or used criminal force` IS A BOOLEAN, `connected with the target's security duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or ought to have known the target was a security officer on duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17A is committed` IF
    `assaulted or used criminal force` AND `connected with the target's security duty` AND `knew or ought to have known the target was a security officer on duty`

-- s 17C(1) (as amended by Act 23 of 2025 wef 29 June 2026): an individual must not use "threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or
-- indecent words or behaviour" or communication towards a security officer "in relation to the execution of" the duty, "with the
-- intent to cause harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation ... and as a result causing" it.
-- (3) defence, proved on a balance of probabilities: (a) did not know and had no reason to believe it would be perceived by the
-- target; or (b) "the accused's conduct was reasonable".
-- (4) no protection where the target is "also a public service worker" under the Protection from Harassment Act 2014 and acting as
-- such. s 17E knowledge requirement applies.
DECLARE Harassment HAS
    `threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent words, behaviour or communication` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in relation to the target's security duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intended harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew or ought to have known the target was a security officer on duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `target was acting as a public service worker` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accused proved no reason to believe the target would perceive it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accused proved the conduct was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the incident` IS A Harassment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17C is committed` IF
        `the incident`'s `threatening, abusive, insulting, sexual or indecent words, behaviour or communication`
    AND `the incident`'s `in relation to the target's security duty`
    AND `the incident`'s `intended harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND `the incident`'s `caused harassment, alarm, distress or humiliation`
    AND `the incident`'s `knew or ought to have known the target was a security officer on duty`
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `target was acting as a public service worker`)
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `accused proved no reason to believe the target would perceive it`)
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `accused proved the conduct was reasonable`)

-- s 17D: an individual previously convicted under the repealed ss 13A to 13D of the Miscellaneous Offences (Public Order and
-- Nuisance) Act 1906, ss 3 to 7 of the Protection from Harassment Act 2014, or s 17C, is liable on a subsequent s 17C conviction to
-- "$10,000 or ... 2 years". Otherwise s 17C(2): $5,000 or 12 months.
GIVEN `has a prior harassment conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 17C maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `has a prior harassment conviction` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `has a prior harassment conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 17C maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `has a prior harassment conviction` THEN 24 ELSE 12

-- s 28(1): the licensing officer may arrest without warrant for any offence under the Act "other than an offence under section
-- 17A, 17B or 17C". (1A): those three are "non-arrestable" unless a person offends "in the view of a police officer".
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `committed in the view of a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is treated as arrestable by the police` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `assaulting a security officer` THEN `committed in the view of a police officer`
    WHEN `hurting a security officer` THEN `committed in the view of a police officer`
    WHEN `harassing a security officer` THEN `committed in the view of a police officer`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `18, 19 -- security service providers`

-- s 18(1): a person provides a security service by (a) installing, maintaining, repairing or servicing security equipment; (b)
-- "designing, selling, importing or exporting ... any security equipment (other than basic household or automotive security items at
-- approved classes of retail outlets or intruder alarm systems)"; (c) "providing product advice in relation to security equipment,
-- other than basic household or automotive security items at approved classes of retail outlets"; (f) selling, or (g) using in
-- cash-in-transit, an intelligent banknote neutralisation system; (h) alarm surveillance or monitoring with security equipment; (i)
-- training in any of those; (j) providing persons to do them.
-- s 18(2): no one provides a security service "only because the person sells self-install security systems".
-- The Schedule lists "Intruder alarm systems" (item 7) as security equipment, so installing one is (a), but selling one falls in the
-- (b)(i) carve-out. Product advice on one is not carved out of (c).
DECLARE SecurityActivity IS ONE OF
    `installing CCTV in an office`
    `servicing an intruder alarm system`
    `selling an intruder alarm system`
    `selling CCTV cameras to businesses`
    `selling basic household security items at an approved retail outlet`
    `selling self-install security systems only`
    `advising a client on which intruder alarm to buy`
    `advising on basic household security items at an approved retail outlet`
    `selling a banknote neutralisation system`
    `monitoring alarms for clients`
    `training alarm installers`
    `supplying technicians to install security equipment`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A SecurityActivity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is a security service` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `selling an intruder alarm system` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `selling basic household security items at an approved retail outlet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `selling self-install security systems only` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `advising on basic household security items at an approved retail outlet` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 19(1): no one may "engage in the business of providing, for reward, any security service" without a security service provider's
-- licence. (2) $10,000 or 2 years.
GIVEN `the activity` IS A SecurityActivity, `in business for reward` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a security service provider's licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 19 is contravened` IF
        `the activity is a security service` `the activity`
    AND `in business for reward`
    AND (NOT `holds a security service provider's licence`)

§§ `20 -- false alarms`

-- s 20(2): "a false alarm is the activation of an alarm system by reasons other than fire or intruders".
-- (3): the charge for police attendance "is payable by a prescribed licensed security service provider" where (a) it installed or
-- maintained the alarm system and (b) "the licensing officer is satisfied that [it] had failed to take all reasonably practicable
-- measures to verify whether the activation ... is a false alarm before making or causing the call to be made".
-- (6): "alarm system" excludes "an alarm installed in a vehicle or a personal alarm attached to the body of an individual".
DECLARE AlarmCall HAS
    `police attended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `activated by fire or intruders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a vehicle or personal alarm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider installed or maintained the system` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider is of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN
    `provider failed to take reasonably practicable steps to verify` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the call` IS AN AlarmCall
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider is liable for the false-alarm charge` IF
        `the call`'s `police attended`
    AND (NOT `the call`'s `activated by fire or intruders`)
    AND (NOT `the call`'s `a vehicle or personal alarm`)
    AND `the call`'s `provider installed or maintained the system`
    AND `the call`'s `provider is of a prescribed class`
    AND `the call`'s `provider failed to take reasonably practicable steps to verify`

-- s 20(4): a person who "(a) intentionally gives a false alarm of fire or intruder; or (b) is reckless about whether it would cause a
-- person to fear that there is a fire or an intruder, or cause an emergency service to respond" -- $5,000 or 6 months.
-- The deposited text does not repeat "gives a false alarm" in (b); read naively, (b) is satisfied by the recklessness alone. This
-- encoding requires a false alarm in both limbs (an inference about the drafting).
GIVEN `gave a false alarm of fire or intruder` IS A BOOLEAN, `intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN, `recklessly as to fear or emergency response` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20(4) is committed` IF
    `gave a false alarm of fire or intruder` AND (`intentionally` OR `recklessly as to fear or emergency response`)

§§ `23, 24, 26 -- validity, suspension and appeal`

-- s 23(c): a licence is valid "for such period (not exceeding 5 years) as may be specified in the licence".
GIVEN `years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence period is permitted` IF
    `years` GREATER THAN 0 AND `years` AT MOST 5

-- s 24(2)(a): where revocation is not warranted, the licensing officer may "suspend the licence for a period not exceeding 6
-- months". s 24(7)(b) likewise caps a suspension after an immediate suspension at 6 months.
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension period is permitted` IF
    `months` GREATER THAN 0 AND `months` AT MOST 6

-- s 24(3): no revocation or suspension "unless an opportunity of being heard ... had been given to the licensee"; s 24(5) lets the
-- officer suspend a private investigator's or security officer's licence immediately "despite subsection (3)" where the licensee
-- has been charged with or convicted of a prescribed offence.
DECLARE LicenceKind IS ONE OF
    `a private investigator's licence`
    `a private investigation agency's licence`
    `a security officer's licence`
    `a security agency's licence`
    `a security service provider's licence`

GIVEN `the licence` IS A LicenceKind, `charged with or convicted of a prescribed offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `immediate suspension without a hearing is available` IF
    `charged with or convicted of a prescribed offence` AND
    (CONSIDER `the licence`
     WHEN `a private investigator's licence` THEN TRUE
     WHEN `a security officer's licence` THEN TRUE
     OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- s 24(9): an order "revoking or suspending a private investigator's licence or security officer's licence does not take effect
-- until the expiry of 14 days after notice has been served". s 26(5): if the licensee appeals to the Minister, the order "does not
-- take effect unless the order is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is ... dismissed ... or withdrawn".
-- s 24(9) names only those two licences; for agency and provider licences the Act gives no deferral (the encoding returns the day of
-- service, an inference from silence).
GIVEN `the licence` IS A LicenceKind, `notice served on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earliest day the order takes effect without an appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the licence`
    WHEN `a private investigator's licence` THEN `notice served on day` PLUS 14
    WHEN `a security officer's licence` THEN `notice served on day` PLUS 14
    OTHERWISE `notice served on day`

GIVEN `appealed` IS A BOOLEAN, `appeal confirmed, dismissed or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appealed order may take effect` IF
    (NOT `appealed`) OR `appeal confirmed, dismissed or withdrawn`

-- s 26(1)-(3): appeals to the Minister against refusals, conditions and orders must be brought "within 14 days" after notification or
-- service, to "the Minister whose decision is final". s 24(6): review of an immediate suspension may be sought "within 14 days".
GIVEN `days since notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `days since notified` AT MOST 14

§§ `33 -- composition`

-- s 33(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence"; or (b) "$2,000". Which offences are compoundable is left to regulations.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `35 -- no fees without a licence`

-- s 35: a person providing the service of a private investigator, agency, security officer, security agency or security service
-- provider "shall not be entitled to bring any proceeding in any court to recover any commission, fee, gain or reward ... unless,
-- at the time of providing the service, the person is the holder of a valid" licence of that kind.
-- The test is the licence held at the time of the service; one obtained later does not cure it.
GIVEN `licensed when the service was provided` IS A BOOLEAN, `licensed when suing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may sue for the fee` IF
    `licensed when the service was provided`
